# superpowers brainstorming companion (transient mockups)
.superpowers/

# Specification PDFs (USB-IF, NXP, ...). Kept out of git for the same reason
# the parent rt1170/ directory is: they are large and copyrighted. The USB-IF
# ones carry "A LICENSE IS HEREBY GRANTED TO REPRODUCE THIS SPECIFICATION FOR
# INTERNAL USE ONLY" on their notice page, so publishing them in a public
# repo would breach the licence they were downloaded under. Cite clause
# numbers in code and docs; keep the documents local.
docs/*.pdf

# Gate monitor sockets (cm4_usb_irq_probe hotplugs via -monitor unix:).
# Trap-cleaned on normal exit; this covers a SIGKILLed run leaving one behind.
*.sock

# Bench-AP credentials, generated from the RT1176 build cache. NEVER committed
# -- this repo already leaked live Wi-Fi passwords once (W6, still in pushed
# history), so the generated header is ignored before it is ever created.
tools/esp32c6-benchap/ap_creds.h
